-- Fill empty model descriptions and remove stale "latest"/"flagship" wording.
--
-- 1. 26 active models had no description. The new text comes from each
--    vendor's own documentation (Recraft, Microsoft MAI, Voyage, Inception,
--    Perplexity, Liquid AI, Google); facts that could not be verified from a
--    vendor source (for example context limits) were left out.
-- 2. Descriptions that call a model "the latest", "newest" or "most capable"
--    even though a newer model exists now say when the model was released
--    instead, and retired models are described in the past tense. Other facts
--    in each description are untouched. deepseek/deepseek-v3-0324 held
--    DeepSeek R1 text; it now uses the DeepSeek V3 text from its sibling row
--    deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324 (same 2025-03-24 snapshot).

-- Guarded on the description observed during the 2026-10-12 audit, so a newer
-- admin edit is never overwritten. Row-level history is recorded by the
-- catalogue_row_history trigger on public.v2_models.
with fixes (model_slug, old_description, new_description) as (
values
  ($d$google/antigravity-preview-09-2026$d$::text, null::text, $d$Antigravity Preview (September 2026) is a managed agent from Google for autonomous, multi-step workflows. It plans, reasons, executes code, handles files and searches the web in a Google-hosted isolated Linux sandbox, with text and image input, text output, and a 1,048,576-token context window.$d$::text),
  ($d$inception/mercury-decide$d$::text, null::text, $d$Mercury Decide is a structured decision model from Inception for classification, routing and scoring. It evaluates named yes/no, choice or score questions against a shared text or JSON state and returns typed answers with probabilities instead of generated text.$d$::text),
  ($d$inception/mercury-decide:free$d$::text, null::text, $d$Mercury Decide (Free) is a structured decision model from Inception for classification, routing and scoring. It evaluates named yes/no, choice or score questions against a shared text or JSON state and returns typed answers with probabilities instead of generated text.$d$::text),
  ($d$liquid-ai/d1:free$d$::text, null::text, $d$D1 (Free) is a decision model from Liquid AI for classification, routing and scoring. It reads text and images together with typed yes/no, choice or score questions and returns probabilities in a single pass without generating any tokens.$d$::text),
  ($d$microsoft/mai-voice-2.1-flash$d$::text, null::text, $d$MAI-Voice-2.1-Flash is a text-to-speech model from Microsoft for low-latency, real-time speech generation. It produces expressive speech across 23 languages with emotion and style control through SSML, and supports gated instant voice cloning.$d$::text),
  ($d$microsoft/mai-voice-2.1$d$::text, null::text, $d$MAI-Voice-2.1 is a text-to-speech model from Microsoft for expressive, high-fidelity speech generation. It supports 23 languages, SSML emotion and style control, gated instant voice cloning, and long-form generation that keeps speaker consistency across audiobooks, podcasts and narration.$d$::text),
  ($d$microsoft/mai-transcribe-2-streaming$d$::text, null::text, $d$MAI-Transcribe-2-Streaming is a low-latency speech-to-text model from Microsoft for real-time transcription. Audio is sent as a continuous stream and incremental transcripts are returned while the speaker talks, with intermediate results updated and final results confirming each segment.$d$::text),
  ($d$microsoft/mai-image-2.6-flash$d$::text, null::text, $d$MAI-Image-2.6-Flash is a diffusion-based image generation and editing model from Microsoft with the same text-to-image and image-to-image capabilities as MAI-Image-2.6, offered as a faster variant. Prompts can be up to 32,000 tokens, and edits accept up to five reference images.$d$::text),
  ($d$microsoft/mai-image-2.6$d$::text, null::text, $d$MAI-Image-2.6 is a diffusion-based image generation and editing model from Microsoft for text-to-image generation and image-to-image edits. Prompts can be up to 32,000 tokens, edits accept up to five reference images, and output is PNG up to 2,359,296 total pixels.$d$::text),
  ($d$microsoft/mai-transcribe-2$d$::text, null::text, $d$MAI-Transcribe-2 is a speech-to-text model from Microsoft for transcribing audio files across 60 languages. It provides speaker diarization, word-level timestamps, automatic language identification, keyword biasing, code switching, and clean or verbatim transcription styles.$d$::text),
  ($d$perplexity/decider-27b$d$::text, null::text, $d$Decider 27B is a decision model from Perplexity that answers typed yes/no, choice and score questions with probabilities instead of generated text. It accepts text, JSON or image input with up to 262,144 tokens per request.$d$::text),
  ($d$recraft/recraft-v4.1-vector$d$::text, null::text, $d$Recraft V4.1 VECTOR is a vector image generation model from Recraft for creating logos, typography and illustrations. It returns editable SVG output.$d$::text),
  ($d$recraft/recraft-v4.1-pro$d$::text, null::text, $d$Recraft V4.1 Pro is a raster image generation model from Recraft that generates at 2K resolution with finer detail than the standard V4.1 model. It is aimed at print-ready and large-scale assets.$d$::text),
  ($d$recraft/recraft-v4.1-pro-vector$d$::text, null::text, $d$Recraft V4.1 Pro VECTOR is the Pro vector variant of Recraft V4.1 from Recraft, which returns editable SVG for logos, typography and illustration.$d$::text),
  ($d$recraft/recraft-v4.1$d$::text, null::text, $d$Recraft V4.1 is a text-to-image model from Recraft that produces 1K raster images with strong photorealism and prompt following. It is the default model in Recraft's API and also supports image-to-image.$d$::text),
  ($d$recraft/recraft-v4.1-utility$d$::text, null::text, $d$Recraft V4.1 Utility is a raster image generation model from Recraft that trades the main line's artistic point of view for predictability. It produces clean images with flat lighting, front-facing composition and simple scenes, suited to mockups and product listing photos.$d$::text),
  ($d$recraft/recraft-v4.1-utility-vector$d$::text, null::text, $d$Recraft V4.1 Utility VECTOR is the vector variant of Recraft V4.1 Utility from Recraft, returning editable SVG with clean, predictable results, flat lighting and simple composition.$d$::text),
  ($d$recraft/recraft-v4.1-utility-pro$d$::text, null::text, $d$Recraft V4.1 Utility Pro is the Pro variant of Recraft V4.1 Utility from Recraft, a raster model for clean, predictable images with flat lighting and simple composition at 2K resolution.$d$::text),
  ($d$recraft/recraft-v4.1-utility-pro-vector$d$::text, null::text, $d$Recraft V4.1 Utility Pro VECTOR is the Pro vector variant of Recraft V4.1 Utility from Recraft, returning editable SVG with clean, predictable results, flat lighting and simple composition.$d$::text),
  ($d$recraft/recraft-v4.1-flash$d$::text, null::text, $d$Recraft V4.1 Flash is a raster text-to-image model from Recraft built for high-volume generation and rapid iteration, with quality close to Recraft V4.1. It outputs 1K images and does not support style parameters, vector output or image-to-image.$d$::text),
  ($d$recraft/recraft-v4-styles$d$::text, null::text, $d$Recraft V4 Styles is a style-consistent image generation model from Recraft that matches the look of one to ten reference images, with no training or fine-tuning. It always requires a style ID or style reference images and offers Precise and Flexible matching modes.$d$::text),
  ($d$recraft/recraft-v4-styles-vector$d$::text, null::text, $d$Recraft V4 Styles VECTOR is the vector variant of Recraft V4 Styles from Recraft, generating SVG output that matches the look of one to ten reference images.$d$::text),
  ($d$recraft/recraft-v4-styles-pro$d$::text, null::text, $d$Recraft V4 Styles Pro is the higher-resolution variant of Recraft V4 Styles from Recraft, generating images that match the look of one to ten reference images.$d$::text),
  ($d$recraft/recraft-v4-styles-pro-vector$d$::text, null::text, $d$Recraft V4 Styles Pro VECTOR is the Pro vector variant of Recraft V4 Styles from Recraft, generating SVG output that matches the look of one to ten reference images.$d$::text),
  ($d$voyage/rerank-3$d$::text, null::text, $d$Rerank 3 is a reranking model from Voyage AI that scores and reorders candidate documents by relevance to a query. It has a 32K-token context length and supports instruction-following.$d$::text),
  ($d$voyage/rerank-3-lite$d$::text, null::text, $d$Rerank 3 Lite is a reranking model from Voyage AI that scores and reorders candidate documents by relevance to a query, optimized for latency-sensitive applications. It has a 32K-token context length and supports instruction-following.$d$::text),
  ($d$alibaba/wan-2.6$d$::text, $d$Alibaba's most advanced video generation model, supporting over 10 visual creation capabilities in a unified system. Wan 2.6 generates 1080p video at 24fps from text, images, reference videos, or audio,...$d$::text, $d$Alibaba's video generation model, released in March 2026, supporting over 10 visual creation capabilities in a unified system. Wan 2.6 generates 1080p video at 24fps from text, images, reference videos, or audio,...$d$::text),
  ($d$deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324$d$::text, $d$DeepSeek V3, a 685B-parameter, mixture-of-experts model, is the latest iteration of the flagship chat model family from the DeepSeek team. It succeeds the [DeepSeek V3](/deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3) model and performs really well...$d$::text, $d$DeepSeek V3, a 685B-parameter, mixture-of-experts model, is the March 2025 iteration of the chat model family from the DeepSeek team. It succeeds the [DeepSeek V3](/deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3) model and performs really well...$d$::text),
  ($d$meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct$d$::text, $d$Meta's latest class of models, Llama 3.1, launched with a variety of sizes and configurations. The 8B instruct-tuned version is particularly fast and efficient. It has demonstrated strong performance in human evaluations, outperforming several leading closed-source models.$d$::text, $d$Meta's Llama 3.1 class of models, launched in July 2024 with a variety of sizes and configurations. The 8B instruct-tuned version is particularly fast and efficient. It has demonstrated strong performance in human evaluations, outperforming several leading closed-source models.$d$::text),
  ($d$meta/llama-3.1-70b-instruct$d$::text, $d$Meta's latest class of model (Llama 3.1) launched with a variety of sizes & flavors. This 70B instruct-tuned version is optimized for high quality dialogue usecases. It has demonstrated strong...$d$::text, $d$Meta's Llama 3.1 class of model, launched in July 2024 with a variety of sizes & flavors. This 70B instruct-tuned version is optimized for high quality dialogue usecases. It has demonstrated strong...$d$::text),
  ($d$mistral/mistral-large-2407$d$::text, $d$This is Mistral AI's flagship model, Mistral Large 2 (version mistral-large-2407). It's a proprietary weights-available model and excels at reasoning, code, JSON, chat, and more. Read the launch announcement [here](https://mistral.ai/news/mistral-large-2407/)....$d$::text, $d$This is Mistral AI's Mistral Large 2 model (version mistral-large-2407). It's a proprietary weights-available model and excels at reasoning, code, JSON, chat, and more. Read the launch announcement [here](https://mistral.ai/news/mistral-large-2407/)....$d$::text),
  ($d$openai/gpt-5.4-pro$d$::text, $d$GPT 5.4 Pro is OpenAI's most advanced model, building on GPT-5.4's unified architecture with enhanced reasoning capabilities for complex, high-stakes tasks.$d$::text, $d$GPT 5.4 Pro is OpenAI's Pro-tier model, released in March 2026, building on GPT-5.4's unified architecture with enhanced reasoning capabilities for complex, high-stakes tasks.$d$::text),
  ($d$openai/gpt-5.4$d$::text, $d$GPT 5.4 is OpenAI's latest frontier model, unifying the Codex and GPT lines into a single system. It supports up to 1.1M of input context for long documents, codebases, and agent workflows.$d$::text, $d$GPT 5.4 is an OpenAI model, released in March 2026, that unifies the Codex and GPT lines into a single system. It supports up to 1.1M of input context for long documents, codebases, and agent workflows.$d$::text),
  ($d$openai/gpt-5.2-pro$d$::text, $d$GPT 5.2 Pro is OpenAI's most advanced model, offering major improvements in agentic coding and long context performance over GPT-5 Pro. It targets higher-capability workloads where depth, quality, or scale matter more than raw speed.$d$::text, $d$GPT 5.2 Pro is OpenAI's Pro-tier model, released in December 2025, offering major improvements in agentic coding and long context performance over GPT-5 Pro. It targets higher-capability workloads where depth, quality, or scale matter more than raw speed.$d$::text),
  ($d$openai/gpt-5.2$d$::text, $d$GPT 5.2 is the latest frontier-grade model in the GPT-5 series, offering stronger agentic and long context perfomance compared to GPT-5.1. It accepts text and image inputs and produces text outputs.$d$::text, $d$GPT 5.2 is a frontier-grade model in the GPT-5 series released in December 2025, offering stronger agentic and long context perfomance compared to GPT-5.1. It accepts text and image inputs and produces text outputs.$d$::text),
  ($d$openai/gpt-4.1$d$::text, $d$GPT 4.1 is a flagship large language model optimized for advanced instruction following, real-world software engineering, and long-context reasoning. It supports up to 1.0M of input context for long documents, codebases, and agent workflows.$d$::text, $d$GPT 4.1 is a large language model, released in April 2025, optimized for advanced instruction following, real-world software engineering, and long-context reasoning. It supports up to 1.0M of input context for long documents, codebases, and agent workflows.$d$::text),
  ($d$openai/gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18$d$::text, $d$GPT-4o mini is OpenAI's newest model after [GPT-4 Omni](/models/openai/gpt-4o), supporting both text and image inputs with text outputs. As their most advanced small model, it is many multiples more affordable...$d$::text, $d$GPT-4o mini is an OpenAI model released in July 2024 after [GPT-4 Omni](/models/openai/gpt-4o), supporting both text and image inputs with text outputs. As their small model, it is many multiples more affordable...$d$::text),
  ($d$openai/gpt-4o-mini$d$::text, $d$GPT 4o Mini (2024-07-18) is OpenAI's newest model after [GPT-4 Omni](/models/openai/gpt-4o), supporting both text and image inputs with text outputs. It is a smaller-footprint option suited to tighter latency or deployment budgets.$d$::text, $d$GPT 4o Mini (2024-07-18) is an OpenAI model released in July 2024 after [GPT-4 Omni](/models/openai/gpt-4o), supporting both text and image inputs with text outputs. It is a smaller-footprint option suited to tighter latency or deployment budgets.$d$::text),
  ($d$qwen/qwen3.7-max-preview$d$::text, $d$Qwen 3.7 Max Preview is a preview Qwen frontier text-generation model for reasoning and chat workloads. It accepts text-only input, enables thinking mode by default, and does not expose the cache features available on the stable 2026-05-20 release.$d$::text, $d$Qwen 3.7 Max Preview is a preview Qwen text-generation model for reasoning and chat workloads. It accepts text-only input, enables thinking mode by default, and does not expose the cache features available on the stable 2026-05-20 release.$d$::text),
  ($d$qwen/qwen-plus$d$::text, $d$Qwen3, the latest generation in the Qwen large language model series, features both dense and mixture-of-experts (MoE) architectures to excel in reasoning, multilingual support, and advanced agent tasks. Its unique ability to switch seamlessly between a thinking mode for complex reasoning and a non-thinking mode for efficient dialogue ensures versatile, high-quality performance.

Significantly outperforming prior models like QwQ and Qwen2.5, Qwen3 delivers superior mathematics, coding, commonsense reasoning, creative writing, and interactive dialogue capabilities. The Qwen3-30B-A3B variant includes 30.5 billion parameters (3.3 billion activated), 48 layers, 128 experts (8 activated per task), and supports up to 131K token contexts with YaRN, setting a new standard among open-source models.$d$::text, $d$Qwen3, a generation in the Qwen large language model series, features both dense and mixture-of-experts (MoE) architectures to excel in reasoning, multilingual support, and advanced agent tasks. Its unique ability to switch seamlessly between a thinking mode for complex reasoning and a non-thinking mode for efficient dialogue ensures versatile, high-quality performance.

Significantly outperforming prior models like QwQ and Qwen2.5, Qwen3 delivers superior mathematics, coding, commonsense reasoning, creative writing, and interactive dialogue capabilities. The Qwen3-30B-A3B variant includes 30.5 billion parameters (3.3 billion activated), 48 layers, 128 experts (8 activated per task), and supports up to 131K token contexts with YaRN, setting a new standard among open-source models.$d$::text),
  ($d$spacex-ai/grok-4.6$d$::text, $d$Grok 4.6 is SpaceXAI's frontier model for coding, agentic tasks, and knowledge work. It supports text and image input, a 500k-token context window, configurable reasoning, function calling, structured outputs, and xAI's server-side web search, X search, and code execution tools.$d$::text, $d$Grok 4.6 is SpaceXAI's model for coding, agentic tasks, and knowledge work. It supports text and image input, a 500k-token context window, configurable reasoning, function calling, structured outputs, and xAI's server-side web search, X search, and code execution tools.$d$::text),
  ($d$spacex-ai/grok-4.2-beta$d$::text, $d$Grok 4.20 Beta is xAI's newest flagship model with industry-leading speed and agentic tool calling capabilities. It combines the lowest hallucination rate on the market with strict prompt adherance, delivering consistently precise and truthful responses.$d$::text, $d$Grok 4.20 Beta is an xAI model released in March 2026 with industry-leading speed and agentic tool calling capabilities. It combines the lowest hallucination rate on the market with strict prompt adherance, delivering consistently precise and truthful responses.$d$::text),
  ($d$spacex-ai/grok-4-fast-non-reasoning$d$::text, $d$Grok 4 Fast Non Reasoning is SpaceXAI's best agentic tool calling model that shines in real-world use cases like customer support and deep research. 2M context window.$d$::text, $d$Grok 4 Fast Non Reasoning is a SpaceXAI agentic tool calling model that shines in real-world use cases like customer support and deep research. 2M context window.$d$::text),
  ($d$spacex-ai/grok-4-fast-reasoning$d$::text, $d$Grok 4 Fast Reasoning is SpaceXAI's best agentic tool calling model that shines in real-world use cases like customer support and deep research. 2M context window.$d$::text, $d$Grok 4 Fast Reasoning is a SpaceXAI agentic tool calling model that shines in real-world use cases like customer support and deep research. 2M context window.$d$::text),
  ($d$spacex-ai/grok-4-fast$d$::text, $d$xAI's latest advancement in cost-efficient reasoning models$d$::text, $d$xAI's September 2025 advancement in cost-efficient reasoning models$d$::text),
  ($d$z-ai/glm-5.2$d$::text, $d$GLM 5.2 is Z.AI's frontier open-weights model for coding and long-horizon agentic tasks, with a 1M context window and high/max reasoning effort controls.$d$::text, $d$GLM 5.2 is Z.AI's open-weights model for coding and long-horizon agentic tasks, with a 1M context window and high/max reasoning effort controls.$d$::text),
  ($d$z-ai/glm-5$d$::text, $d$GLM 5 is Z.ai's flagship open-source foundation model engineered for complex systems design and long-horizon agent workflows. It accepts text inputs and produces text outputs.$d$::text, $d$GLM 5 is Z.ai's open-source foundation model engineered for complex systems design and long-horizon agent workflows. It accepts text inputs and produces text outputs.$d$::text),
  ($d$z-ai/glm-4.7$d$::text, $d$GLM 4.7 is Z.ai's latest flagship model, featuring upgrades in two key areas: enhanced programming capabilities and more stable multi-step reasoning/execution.$d$::text, $d$GLM 4.7 is a Z.ai model released in December 2025, featuring upgrades in two key areas: enhanced programming capabilities and more stable multi-step reasoning/execution.$d$::text),
  ($d$z-ai/glm-4.5$d$::text, $d$GLM 4.5 is our latest flagship foundation model, purpose-built for agent-based applications. It leverages a Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) architecture and supports a context length of up to 128k tokens.$d$::text, $d$GLM 4.5 is our foundation model, released in July 2025, purpose-built for agent-based applications. It leverages a Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) architecture and supports a context length of up to 128k tokens.$d$::text),
  ($d$deepseek/deepseek_v3$d$::text, $d$DeepSeek-V3 is the latest model from the DeepSeek team, building upon the instruction following and coding abilities of the previous versions. Pre-trained on nearly 15 trillion tokens, the reported evaluations reveal that the model outperforms other open-source models and rivals leading closed-source models.$d$::text, $d$DeepSeek-V3 was a model from the DeepSeek team, building upon the instruction following and coding abilities of the previous versions. Pre-trained on nearly 15 trillion tokens, the reported evaluations revealed that the model outperformed other open-source models and rivaled leading closed-source models.$d$::text),
