  ($d$openai/gpt-5.1-codex-max$d$::text, $d$GPT 5.1 Codex Max is OpenAI's latest agentic coding model, designed for long-running, high-context software development tasks. It targets higher-capability workloads where depth, quality, or scale matter more than raw speed.$d$::text, $d$GPT 5.1 Codex Max was an OpenAI agentic coding model, released in November 2025, designed for long-running, high-context software development tasks. It targeted higher-capability workloads where depth, quality, or scale mattered more than raw speed.$d$::text),
  ($d$openai/gpt-5.1$d$::text, $d$GPT 5.1 is the latest frontier-grade model in the GPT-5 series, offering stronger general-purpose reasoning, improved instruction adherence, and a more natural conversational style compared to GPT-5.$d$::text, $d$GPT 5.1 is a frontier-grade model in the GPT-5 series released in November 2025, offering stronger general-purpose reasoning, improved instruction adherence, and a more natural conversational style compared to GPT-5.$d$::text),
  ($d$openai/gpt-4o-2024-05-13$d$::text, $d$GPT 4o (2024-05-13) is OpenAI's latest AI model, supporting both text and image inputs with text outputs. It accepts text and image inputs and produces text outputs.$d$::text, $d$GPT 4o (2024-05-13) is an OpenAI model, released in May 2024, supporting both text and image inputs with text outputs. It accepts text and image inputs and produces text outputs.$d$::text),
  ($d$poolside/laguna-m.1:free$d$::text, $d$Laguna M.1 is Poolside's flagship 225B total parameter agentic coding model for long-horizon work, now available as open weights on Hugging Face under Apache 2.0.$d$::text, $d$Laguna M.1 is Poolside's 225B total parameter agentic coding model for long-horizon work, released as open weights on Hugging Face under Apache 2.0.$d$::text),
  ($d$poolside/laguna-m.1$d$::text, $d$Laguna M.1 is Poolside's flagship 225B total parameter agentic coding model for long-horizon work, now available as open weights on Hugging Face under Apache 2.0.$d$::text, $d$Laguna M.1 is Poolside's 225B total parameter agentic coding model for long-horizon work, released as open weights on Hugging Face under Apache 2.0.$d$::text),
  ($d$qwen/qwen-2.5-coder-32b-instruct$d$::text, $d$Qwen2.5-Coder is the latest series of Code-Specific Qwen large language models (formerly known as CodeQwen). Qwen2.5-Coder brings the following improvements upon CodeQwen1.5: - Significantly improvements in **code generation**, **code reasoning**...$d$::text, $d$Qwen2.5-Coder was a series of Code-Specific Qwen large language models (formerly known as CodeQwen). Qwen2.5-Coder brought the following improvements upon CodeQwen1.5: - Significantly improvements in **code generation**, **code reasoning**...$d$::text),
  ($d$qwen/qwen-2.5-72b-instruct$d$::text, $d$Qwen2.5 is the latest series of Qwen large language models. For Qwen2.5, we release a number of base language models and instruction-tuned language models ranging from 0.5 to 72 billion parameters.$d$::text, $d$Qwen2.5 was a series of Qwen large language models. For Qwen2.5, we released a number of base language models and instruction-tuned language models ranging from 0.5 to 72 billion parameters.$d$::text),
  ($d$spacex-ai/grok-4$d$::text, $d$Grok 4 is SpaceXAI's latest reasoning model with a 256k context window. It supports parallel tool calling, structured outputs, and both image and text inputs.$d$::text, $d$Grok 4 was a SpaceXAI reasoning model with a 256k context window. It supported parallel tool calling, structured outputs, and both image and text inputs.$d$::text),
  ($d$spacex-ai/grok-3$d$::text, $d$Grok 3 is the latest model from SpaceXAI. It's their flagship model that excels at enterprise use cases like data extraction, coding, and text summarization.$d$::text, $d$Grok 3 was a model from SpaceXAI. It was their flagship model that excelled at enterprise use cases like data extraction, coding, and text summarization.$d$::text),
  ($d$spacex-ai/grok-3-beta$d$::text, $d$Grok 3 Beta is the latest model from SpaceXAI. It's their flagship model that excels at enterprise use cases like data extraction, coding, and text summarization.$d$::text, $d$Grok 3 Beta is a model from SpaceXAI that excels at enterprise use cases like data extraction, coding, and text summarization.$d$::text),
  ($d$deepseek/deepseek-v3-0324$d$::text, $d$DeepSeek R1 is the latest open-source model released by the DeepSeek team, featuring impressive reasoning capabilities, particularly achieving performance comparable to OpenAI's o1 model in mathematics, coding, and reasoning tasks.$d$::text, $d$DeepSeek V3, a 685B-parameter, mixture-of-experts model, is the March 2025 iteration of the chat model family from the DeepSeek team. It succeeds the [DeepSeek V3](/deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3) model and performs really well...$d$::text)
), applied as (
  update public.v2_models m
  set description = f.new_description,
      updated_at = now()
  from fixes f
  where m.model_slug = f.model_slug
    and m.description is not distinct from f.old_description
  returning m.model_slug
)
select count(*) as updated_rows, 64 as expected_rows from applied;
